opensim-manfredaabye-helpers
============================

The helpers of the manfredaabye fork of OpenSimSearch, another implementation
than the opensim-helpers of this project: PHP scripts that answer the search
of the viewers and index the data of the regions. Nothing is enabled by
installing the package: the scripts are in /usr/share/opensim-manfredaabye-helpers,
to be served by the web server of your choice.

Needs PHP with curl, xml, xmlrpc and MySQL (the package depends on them) and a
MySQL or MariaDB database, on this machine or another one.

1. The database, once, from an administrator account of the server:

     CREATE DATABASE ossearch CHARACTER SET utf8;
     CREATE USER 'ossearch'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<password>';
     GRANT ALL ON ossearch.* TO 'ossearch'@'localhost';

   then its tables:

     mysql ossearch < /usr/share/opensim-manfredaabye-helpers/sql/ossearch.sql

   An existing database is updated with the other file of that folder,
   ossearch-migrations.sql.

2. The settings: /etc/opensim/manfredaabye-helpers/databaseinfo.php (host, account,
   password and name of the database). It is readable by the web server only.

3. The web server: examples/nginx.conf and examples/apache.conf, next to this
   file, serve the folder at /search. Add them to your own configuration, with
   the HTTPS and the host name of your site.

4. OpenSimulator: the simulators register with the service and answer it, in
   their config:

     [Search]
         Module = "OpenSimSearch"
         SearchURL = "https://example.org/search/query.php"

     [DataSnapshot]
         index_sims = true
         data_services = "https://example.org/search/register.php"

   The module is enabled with the others: add opensimsearch to EnabledModules
   in /etc/opensim/opensim.conf (opensim-kit does). For the search of the
   viewers, the grid gives the same address in the [LoginService] of its Robust:

     SearchURL = "https://example.org/search/query.php"

5. The index is filled by parser.php, called regularly, e.g. every 10
   minutes from cron (not installed by the package):

     */10 * * * * www-data curl -fsS http://localhost/search/parser.php >/dev/null

The wiredux folder holds pages for a site built with OpenSim Wiredux (events
and classifieds); the service does not use it.

Errors of the connection to the database go to the error log of PHP.
